WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.291
IEC 62443 is a standards family rather than one checklist.

00:00:04.291 --> 00:00:08.901
Its parts address different subjects and audiences while using related concepts.

00:00:08.901 --> 00:00:13.930
Understanding that structure helps teams select the material relevant to their role

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:18.540
instead of treating one document as the entire industrial cybersecurity program.

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:22.731
The general category establishes shared concepts, terminology, models, and measures.

00:00:22.731 --> 00:00:25.665
These foundations help asset owners, engineers, suppliers,

00:00:25.665 --> 00:00:27.761
and assessors use terms consistently.

00:00:27.761 --> 00:00:31.532
Policies and procedures focus on organizational and operational practices,

00:00:31.532 --> 00:00:34.047
including security programs and service-provider responsibilities.

00:00:34.047 --> 00:00:38.238
System-focused material addresses risk assessment, secure system design, security levels,

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:42.010
and technical requirements for industrial automation and control systems.

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:45.363
This is where concepts such as zones, conduits,

00:00:45.363 --> 00:00:47.877
and system security requirements become central.

00:00:47.877 --> 00:00:52.906
Component-focused material addresses secure product development and technical capabilities for software applications,

00:00:52.906 --> 00:00:55.840
embedded devices, host devices, and network devices.

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:57.517
The categories are connected.

00:00:57.517 --> 00:01:00.869
An asset owner's risk assessment creates system requirements.

00:01:00.869 --> 00:01:05.479
An integrator designs and verifies an architecture that addresses those requirements.

00:01:05.479 --> 00:01:10.090
Product suppliers provide components with appropriate security capabilities and development evidence.

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:13.442
Service providers maintain the system within defined controls.

00:01:13.442 --> 00:01:17.633
A practical implementation starts by identifying applicable roles, lifecycle stages,

00:01:17.633 --> 00:01:18.891
and system boundaries.

00:01:18.891 --> 00:01:24.339
Teams should use the applicable current standards and organizational requirements for detailed work.

00:01:24.339 --> 00:01:26.854
This introductory course explains the framework,

00:01:26.854 --> 00:01:31.464
but it does not substitute for the official documents, project-specific engineering,

00:01:31.464 --> 00:01:33.140
or formal assessment criteria.
